fastPLS system requirements
===========================

fastPLS builds and runs in CPU-only mode by default. CUDA and Apple Metal
support are optional acceleration backends and are not required to install the
package.

CPU-only installation
---------------------

No external GPU software is required. Standard R package installation should
build the CPU implementation on Linux, macOS and Windows.

CUDA installation
-----------------

CUDA support requires an NVIDIA GPU, a compatible NVIDIA driver and the CUDA
Toolkit. To request a CUDA build from source, set FASTPLS_USE_CUDA=1 and set
CUDA_ROOT or CUDA_PATH if the toolkit is not installed in a standard location.

Examples:

  FASTPLS_USE_CUDA=1 CUDA_ROOT=/usr/local/cuda R CMD INSTALL fastPLS

On Windows, CUDA_ROOT can point to a toolkit directory such as:

  C:/Program Files/NVIDIA GPU Computing Toolkit/CUDA/v12.6

If FASTPLS_USE_CUDA is unset, unavailable CUDA software is ignored and the
package builds in CPU-only mode. Set FASTPLS_REQUIRE_CUDA=1 only when a missing
CUDA toolkit should be treated as an installation error.

Apple Metal installation
------------------------

Metal support is available only on macOS with Apple's developer tools. To
request a Metal build from source, set:

  FASTPLS_USE_METAL=1

Bioconductor GPU builds
-----------------------

The package declares optional GPU reliance. Bioconductor builders without GPU
support should build and test the CPU implementation, while GPU-aware builders
can exercise CUDA tests when the required hardware and libraries are available.
